= Batter =

Make the batter by mixing the @plain flour{400%g} and @water{200%ml}. Add extra water as necessary to make a smooth batter without lumps. Add the @eggs{2}(beaten) and @salt{pinch}, and blend together. Add the @spring onions{4}(roughly chopped) and one third of the @white cabbage{400%g}(very finely shredded, excluding core), then mix well. Repeat until all of the cabbage is mixed in and evenly coated with the batter.

= Okonomiyaki =

Heat the frying pan with a thin coating of @sunflower oil{} until smoking, and reduce to a medium heat.

Ladle some of the batter into the centre of the pan to form a circle about 1” thick and 4” diameter.

Sprinkle the surface of the pancake with one-eighth of the @raw prawns{225%g}(heads and shells removed) and @scallops{115%g}. Gently press down using a tablespoon.

When the edge of the pancake is cooked and the surface has started to try, turn it over using two spatulas. Gently press the pancake to stretch it to 6” diameter and half the thickness.

After 2 to ~{3%minutes} turn over again. If the surface is still wet then turn over and cook for another ~{2%minutes}. While the pancake is still in the pan, topping side up, spread on some @Worcestershire sauce{}, @English mustard{}, and @mayonnaise{}. Sprinkle with @kezuri-bushi / katsuobushi{}(dried shaved tuna flakes) and @ao nori{}(dried seaweed flakes).

Keep the pancake warm while making seven more the same way.

Serve hot with a sprinkling of @beni-shoga{}(pickled red ginger) on top.